<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eleazar ben Simon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eleazar ben Simon was a Jewish priest and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zealots">Zealots</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-jewish-roman-war">First Jewish–Roman War</a>. He gained prominence after the defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cestius-gallus">Cestius Gallus</a> in 66, and from 68 his faction held the inner court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-in-jerusalem">Temple in Jerusalem</a>, fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-gischala">John of Gischala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bar-giora">Simon bar Giora</a>. In 70 John's men seized the Temple, and Eleazar's followers were absorbed into his faction before the Roman siege.</p></div>
